  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Of a group of students, 70% study Mathematics, 80% study English and 10% of students study neither of these subjects. If one of these students is randomly selected, find the probability that the student studies:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Mathematics and English",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.6$",
          "worked": "Let $M$ and $E$ denote studying Mathematics and English, respectively.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(M\\cup E)&=1-0.1\\\\\\Pr(M\\cup E)&=0.9\\\\\\Pr(M\\cap E)&=\\Pr(M)+\\Pr(E)-\\Pr(M\\cup E)\\\\\\Pr(M\\cap E)&=0.7+0.8-0.9\\\\\\Pr(M\\cap E)&=0.6\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Mathematics but not English",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.1$",
          "worked": "Using $\\Pr(M\\cap E)=0.6$ from part (a):\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(M\\cap E')&=\\Pr(M)-\\Pr(M\\cap E)\\\\\\Pr(M\\cap E')&=0.7-0.6\\\\\\Pr(M\\cap E')&=0.1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q8-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Mathematics or English",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.9$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(M\\cup E)&=1-\\Pr(M'\\cap E')\\\\\\Pr(M\\cup E)&=1-0.1\\\\\\Pr(M\\cup E)&=0.9\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q8-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Mathematics given that they study English",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.75$",
          "worked": "Restrict the sample space to students studying English.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(M\\mid E)&=\\frac{\\Pr(M\\cap E)}{\\Pr(E)}\\\\\\Pr(M\\mid E)&=\\frac{0.6}{0.8}\\\\\\Pr(M\\mid E)&=0.75\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q8-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Mathematics given that they don’t study English.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.5$",
          "worked": "Restrict the sample space to students not studying English. From part (b), $\\Pr(M\\cap E')=0.1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(E')&=1-0.8\\\\\\Pr(E')&=0.2\\\\\\Pr(M\\mid E')&=\\frac{\\Pr(M\\cap E')}{\\Pr(E')}\\\\\\Pr(M\\mid E')&=\\frac{0.1}{0.2}\\\\\\Pr(M\\mid E')&=0.5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
